--  Flyology uses language-defined Pre and Post aspects, not the historical
--  GNAT Precondition and Postcondition pragmas. GCC 13 documents those as
--  distinct, while Inline_Always requires every direct call to be inlined:
--  https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-13.4.0/gnat_rm/Aspect-Inline_005fAlways.html
--  https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-13.4.0/gnat_rm/Pragma-Precondition.html
--  https://gcc.gnu.org/onlinedocs/gcc-13.4.0/gnat_rm/Pragma-Postcondition.html
--
--  GCC 13.2 through 13.4 emit this diagnostic without distinguishing obsolete
--  frontend inlining from backend inlining, where the checks remain effective
--  as the contract assertion regression verifies. GCC 14 and later contain
--  upstream commit 3754477bb08f12a7866d9f422fad85bac79f2579, which adds the
--  missing Back_End_Inlining condition:
--  https://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/commit/3754477bb08f12a7866d9f422fad85bac79f2579
--
--  This exact GCC 13 suppression hides a false diagnostic, not contract
--  enforcement. It does not make obsolete frontend inlining (-gnatN) safe.
--  Delete it when GCC 13 support is dropped.
pragma Warnings
  (GNAT,
   Off,
   "aspect * not enforced on inlined subprogram *",
   Reason => "Spurious GCC 13 warning fixed upstream by commit 3754477");
